# ┌─ :: SECURITY + ARCHITECTURE :: What a container build may see ──────────────────────────────────
# │ Why : Every Dockerfile builds from the repository root (the deployables share
# │       src/PartnerBank.Security). Whatever is in the build context can be copied into an image
# │       layer by mistake - and an image layer is published to the registry for good.
# │ How : Development secrets, key material, local databases and local build output never enter
# │       the context: a COPY of a whole project folder then cannot carry them into an image.
# │ Ref : doc/Containers.md | OWASP A05 Security Misconfiguration | CWE-798 | CWE-538
# └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ┌─ SEC ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# │ Development settings (the window's secret, demo customers) and key material of any kind,
# │ including IdentityServer's signing keys (keys/).
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.jwk
**/*.password
**/*.cer
**/*.crt
**/keys/
**/smartzipper.exclude.json

# Local SQLite databases: customer accounts and the Partner Bank's data.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# Local build output: the images restore and build their own.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/*.user

# Not part of any image.
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
**/*.zip
doc/
ps/
tools/
tst/